Using this approach as `great_tables` has generic styling support, whereas the `styler` component of `pandas` is only for pandas and `great_tables` is already integrated into `polars`. Hopefully for the next release, both py-shiny and great-tables will be leveraging [`narwhals`](https://github.com/narwhals-dev/narwhals) ("Lightweight and extensible compatibility layer between Polars, pandas, cuDF, Modin, and more"). This way, both py-shiny gets styling support for any data frame package! (Related: #1439)

